    "body":  "Closes #825\n\n## What\nA PagerDuty connector: a person pastes a PagerDuty **User API key** and picks their service region; agents granted the connection get PagerDuty\u0027s hosted MCP tools (incidents, alerts, services, on-call schedules, escalation policies, status pages) as that person.\n\n## Why this shape (`api_key`)\n- PagerDuty\u0027s hosted MCP server (`https://mcp.pagerduty.com/mcp`, EU `https://mcp.eu.pagerduty.com/mcp`) supports OAuth only with a static client and **no dynamic client registration** ([docs](https://support.pagerduty.com/main/docs/pagerduty-mcp-server)). A key needs no operator setup, so the connector works on every server out of the box. A static-OAuth variant can be added later beside it.\n- A **User** key (not General Access) is asked for: some tools (e.g. `list_incidents` scoped to `assigned`/`teams`) need user-level auth, and the identity call `GET https://api.{region}/users/me` names the person (`user.id`, labelled `user.email`). A General Access key has no user and fails that check, which is intended.\n- Region is a choice, never free text, so it can only route to `pagerduty.com` or `eu.pagerduty.com`.\n\n## Rules\n- The key never reaches the coding tool: `token: { kind: pass_through, max_lifetime: null }`, headers are filled by the session host.\n- Least access: PagerDuty has no read-only user key, so `tools: pass_through` (as the loader requires for `api_key`) and the description and skill say plainly that it can write. The skill defaults to read first and confirm before acknowledging/resolving, creating incidents (which pages people), deleting, or posting to a public status page; it treats alert payloads as untrusted.\n- Logo: Simple Icons 16.33.0 `pagerduty` (CC0), viewBox and path only, credited in `NOTICE.md`; brand colour `#06AC38`.\n\n## Tests\n- New `test_the_shipped_pagerduty_entry_signs_in_as_a_user_and_picks_its_region`; catalog, registry and gateway catalog tests updated for the new enabled entry.\n- `pytest tests/switch_core/connections/test_loader.py tests/switch_core/connections/test_registry.py tests/switch_core/gateway/test_connection_catalog.py`: 152 passed locally; the 9 that need Postgres via Docker could not run in my sandbox and are left to CI. `ruff check` clean.\n- Live check: `api.pagerduty.com/users/me`, `api.eu.pagerduty.com/users/me`, `mcp.pagerduty.com/mcp` and `mcp.eu.pagerduty.com/mcp` all answer 401 to a bad key, so the URLs are right.\n\n## Still to do (draft)\n- [ ] Video of connect → grant → agent uses it in a room → grant off (needs a PagerDuty trial account)\n\n_This PR was written by Tali, an AI agent, for the Flip the Switch hackathon._\n",
